      "content": {
        "assertion_mode": "conditional",
        "conditions": [
          "Provisional combined-clause hypothesis (חדא קתני) of 2a:5: finding and whole-ownership wording form one combined claim."
        ],
        "proposition": "Under the provisional combined-clause hypothesis, adding כולה שלי to אני מצאתיה is explained as teaching that sight alone does not acquire; this wording explanation is displaced at 2a:10–11, not the nonacquisition rule.",
        "scope": "Provisional explanation of Mishnah wording at Bava Metzia 2a:6; dependency displaced at Bava Metzia 2a:10–11; no rejection of sight-nonacquisition."
      },
      "evidence": [
